==============================================================================
E  Is the off-reference gap a property of the ANN or of the regressor?
==============================================================================
  Replace the random ANN write by a write that is EXACTLY in the baseline span
  (a genuine parameter direction). A coefficient fitted on one point set must
  then transfer to any other, because the same theta explains both.
  rho(eval; G_in_span) before = 1.000000   (must be 1)
  ||G_in - Phi_eval a|| / ||G_in|| at the EVALUATION points = 1.763e-14
  VERDICT: a write that lies in the baseline span is removed at ANY point set,
  because the fitted coefficient recovers the true parameter direction. The
  off-reference gap in B is therefore specific to a write that is NOT in the
  span: there the coefficient is a least-squares artefact of the reference
  points and carries no meaning elsewhere.

